{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-109156" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $x=5{y}^{3}-10{y}^{2},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-109156" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(5{y}^{3}-10{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})-10\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =15{y}^{2}-20y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{15{y}^{2}-20y}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-109156" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e7d8a2fcc365bbc964b4cac2e8c70317d39fe136a52bfd8c39f123f22c20db9d"} {"question" "q-109156" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-109156" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15y-10{y}^{2}"] ["math" "15{y}^{2}-20y"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{15{y}^{2}-20y}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3y-20{y}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}-10y}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-109156" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{15{y}^{2}-20y}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-312549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $x={y}^{2}-y,$ express $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ as a function of $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-312549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}-y) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y) \\\\  & =2y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2y-1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-312549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e7d8a2fcc365bbc964b4cac2e8c70317d39fe136a52bfd8c39f123f22c20db9d"} {"question" "q-312549" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-312549" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2y-1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-341608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $x=-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+5{y}^{2},$ express $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ as a function of $y.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | ${y}^{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-341608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+5{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-2{y}^{-1}+5{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2})+5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2(-2{y}^{-3})+5(2y) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{y}^{3}}+10y \\\\  & =\\frac{4+10{y}^{4}}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4+10{y}^{4}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-341608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e7d8a2fcc365bbc964b4cac2e8c70317d39fe136a52bfd8c39f123f22c20db9d"} {"question" "q-341608" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-341608" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4+10y^4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-32705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $x=-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+2{y}^{2},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-32705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-2{y}^{-2}+2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =4{y}^{-3}+4y \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{y}^{3}}+4y \\\\  & =\\frac{4+4{y}^{4}}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4+4{y}^{4}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-32705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e7d8a2fcc365bbc964b4cac2e8c70317d39fe136a52bfd8c39f123f22c20db9d"} {"question" "q-32705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-32705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{y}{4+4{y}^{4}}"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{1+{x}^{4}}"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{3}}{1+{y}^{4}}"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4+4{y}^{3}}"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4+4{y}^{4}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-32705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4+4{y}^{4}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170132" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $x=3{y}^{3}-4{y}^{5},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170132" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(3{y}^{3}-4{y}^{5}) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})-4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{5}) \\\\  & =9{y}^{2}-20{y}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{9{y}^{2}-20{y}^{4}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170132" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e7d8a2fcc365bbc964b4cac2e8c70317d39fe136a52bfd8c39f123f22c20db9d"} {"question" "q-170132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3{y}^{2}-4{y}^{4}"] ["math" "9{y}^{2}-20{y}^{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3{y}^{2}-4{y}^{4}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9{y}^{2}-20{y}^{4}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}-{y}^{4}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{9{y}^{2}-20{y}^{4}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-51336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $x=\\frac{2}{y}+\\frac{8}{{y}^{2}},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(3,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-51336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{2}{y}+\\frac{8}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{-1}+8{y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1})+8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-{y}^{-2})+8\\cdot (-2{y}^{-3}) \\\\  & =-2{y}^{-2}-16{y}^{-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{16}{{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2y-16}{{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2y+16}{{y}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2y+16}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(3,2),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(3,2)} & =-\\frac{{2}^{3}}{2(2)+16} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{20} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-51336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e7d8a2fcc365bbc964b4cac2e8c70317d39fe136a52bfd8c39f123f22c20db9d"} {"question" "q-51336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-51336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2}{5}"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{10}"] ["math" "-\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{9}{22}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-51336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $x=y-2{y}^{3},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(1,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y-2{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3}) \\\\  & =1-6{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{1-6{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(1,-1),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(1,-1)} & =\\frac{1}{1-6(-1)^{2}}=-\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e7d8a2fcc365bbc964b4cac2e8c70317d39fe136a52bfd8c39f123f22c20db9d"} {"question" "q-170140" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170140" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{7}"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170140" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-341757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $x=-\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{y}}-2y\\sqrt{y},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(-14,1).$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-14,1)}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-341757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{y}}-2y\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-12{y}^{-1/2}-2y\\cdot {y}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-12{y}^{-1/2}-2{y}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =-12\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1/2})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =-12(-\\frac{1}{2}){y}^{-3/2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}{y}^{1/2} \\\\  & =6{y}^{-3/2}-3{y}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{y\\sqrt{y}}-3\\sqrt{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-3{y}^{2}}{y\\sqrt{y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{y\\sqrt{y}}{6-3{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(-14,1),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-14,1)} & =\\frac{1\\sqrt{1}}{6-3(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-341757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e7d8a2fcc365bbc964b4cac2e8c70317d39fe136a52bfd8c39f123f22c20db9d"} {"question" "q-341757" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-341757" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-32595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $x=2\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{y}},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(5,9).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-32595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{y}}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\sqrt{y})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{1/2})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}-3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-3/2}) \\\\  & ={y}^{-1/2}+\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}+\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}+\\frac{3}{2y\\sqrt{y}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y+3}{2y\\sqrt{y}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{2y\\sqrt{y}}{2y+3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(5,9),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(5,9)} & =\\frac{2(9)\\sqrt{9}}{2(9)+3}=\\frac{18}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-32595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e7d8a2fcc365bbc964b4cac2e8c70317d39fe136a52bfd8c39f123f22c20db9d"} {"question" "q-32595" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-32595" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{18}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{54}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{18}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-32595" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{18}{7}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-341636" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $x=2{y}^{3}+{y}^{2},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(20,2).$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(20,2)}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-341636" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{3}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2(3{y}^{2})+2y \\\\  & =6{y}^{2}+2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{6{y}^{2}+2y}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(20,2),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(20,2)} & =\\frac{1}{6({2}^{2})+2(2)}=\\frac{1}{28}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-341636" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e7d8a2fcc365bbc964b4cac2e8c70317d39fe136a52bfd8c39f123f22c20db9d"} {"question" "q-341636" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-341636" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{28}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a curve $x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}-2{y}^{2},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(-1,1)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}-2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1/2})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-3/2}-2\\cdot (2y) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{y}^{3/2}}-4y \\\\  & =\\frac{-1-8{y}^{5/2}}{2{y}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1+8{y}^{2}\\sqrt{y}}{2y\\sqrt{y}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=-\\frac{2y\\sqrt{y}}{1+8{y}^{2}\\sqrt{y}}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(-1,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-1,1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2(1)\\sqrt{1}}{1+8(1)^{2}\\sqrt{1}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =-\\frac{2}{9}(x-(-1)) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{9}x-\\frac{2}{9}+1 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{9}x+\\frac{7}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e7d8a2fcc365bbc964b4cac2e8c70317d39fe136a52bfd8c39f123f22c20db9d"} {"question" "q-170190" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170190" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-\\frac{2}{9}x+\\frac{5}{9}"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{2}{9}x+\\frac{7}{9}"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{2}{9}x-\\frac{2}{9}"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{9}{2}x+\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{9}{2}x-\\frac{7}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170190" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-\\frac{2}{9}x+\\frac{7}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-32596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a curve $x=\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}-{y}^{2},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(9,3)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-32596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 3{y}^{2}-2y \\\\  & =2{y}^{2}-2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2{y}^{2}-2y}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(9,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(9,3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2(3)^{2}-2(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{1}{12}(x-9) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{12}-\\frac{3}{4}+3 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-32596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e7d8a2fcc365bbc964b4cac2e8c70317d39fe136a52bfd8c39f123f22c20db9d"} {"question" "q-32596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-32596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=12x-27"] ["math" "y=9x+3"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{7}{2}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{7}{4}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{9}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-32596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{9}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-342049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a curve $x=2y-\\frac{6}{y},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,3)?$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-342049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2y-\\frac{6}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2y-6{y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)-6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =2(1)-6(-{y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2+6{y}^{-2} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{6}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{y}^{2}+6}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2{y}^{2}+6}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(4,3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{2(3)^{2}+6} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot (x-4) \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{8}x-\\frac{3}{2}+3 \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{8}x+\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-342049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e7d8a2fcc365bbc964b4cac2e8c70317d39fe136a52bfd8c39f123f22c20db9d"} {"question" "q-342049" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-342049" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3x}{8}+\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-110192" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a curve $x=5{y}^{3}-8{y}^{2}+16,$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(24,2)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-110192" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(5{y}^{3}-8{y}^{2}+16) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})-8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})+16\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(1) \\\\  & =5\\cdot (3{y}^{2})-8\\cdot (2y)+0 \\\\  & =15{y}^{2}-16y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{15{y}^{2}-16y}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(24,2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(24,2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15\\cdot {2}^{2}-16\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{28}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-2 & =\\frac{1}{28}(x-24) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{28}-\\frac{6}{7}+2 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{8}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-110192" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e7d8a2fcc365bbc964b4cac2e8c70317d39fe136a52bfd8c39f123f22c20db9d"} {"question" "q-110192" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-110192" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{x}{18}-\\frac{7}{8}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{16}{7}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{1}{7}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{8}{7}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{8}-\\frac{8}{7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-110192" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{8}{7}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170192" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a curve $x=4{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}-1,$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,1)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170192" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(4{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}-1) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(1) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(1) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (2y)-2{y}^{-3}-0 \\\\  & =8y-\\frac{2}{{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8{y}^{4}-2}{{y}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{8{y}^{4}-2}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(4,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1)^{3}}{8(1)^{4}-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =\\frac{1}{6}(x-4) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{6}-\\frac{2}{3}+1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170192" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e7d8a2fcc365bbc964b4cac2e8c70317d39fe136a52bfd8c39f123f22c20db9d"} {"question" "q-170192" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170192" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=6x-2"] ["math" "y=6x-23"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{6}+\\frac{23}{6}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{x}{6}+\\frac{5}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "q-170192" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{x}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/state.json" "file_sha256" "e0a9a94fb8f77784ad3d3cc3fb31d1bf917cc6afc1b024a238a2fbbaee1de5b2"} {"question" "e-12467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $x=2y^2 + \\dfrac1{y^2}$, then find $\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/example-12467.json" "file_sha256" "ff0abd0441ed4667c164a6baa1b3a73544eebdd5dd79e5945c5f97b3976cdaf4"} {"question" "e-12467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{2}+{y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =4y-2{y}^{-3} \\\\  & =4y-\\frac{2}{{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{y}^{4}-2}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx} = \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy} \\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac{y^3}{4y^4 -2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/example-12467.json" "file_sha256" "ff0abd0441ed4667c164a6baa1b3a73544eebdd5dd79e5945c5f97b3976cdaf4"} {"question" "e-12468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $x = y + 2y\\sqrt y$, find $\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx}$ at the point $\\left(3 , 1\\right).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/example-12468.json" "file_sha256" "e503f6cbc77f219104a634963cd6c430aa4fa5bfdc2ae6614282196fbe9d1356"} {"question" "e-12468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y+2y\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y+2{y}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =1+2\\cdot (\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =1+3{y}^{1/2} \\\\  & =1+3\\sqrt{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx} = \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy} \\right)^{-1} =  \\dfrac{1}{1 + 3\\sqrt y}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(3,1),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(3,1)} & =\\frac{1}{1+3\\sqrt{1}}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/example-12468.json" "file_sha256" "e503f6cbc77f219104a634963cd6c430aa4fa5bfdc2ae6614282196fbe9d1356"} {"question" "e-12469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the equation of the tangent to the curve $x = 2y^2 -y + 1$ at the point $(2,1)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/example-12469.json" "file_sha256" "bacf93b0f0cdfe2da3d8a37ab7b3e5d4968ba4f20e8429467f0ca1dbfaccbe32"} {"question" "e-12469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{2}-y+1) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (2y)-1+0 \\\\  & =4y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx} = \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy} \\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac1{4y - 1}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(2,1)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(2,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4(1)-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =\\frac{1}{3}(x-2) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}+1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/example-12469.json" "file_sha256" "bacf93b0f0cdfe2da3d8a37ab7b3e5d4968ba4f20e8429467f0ca1dbfaccbe32"} {"question" "q-32595" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{18}{7}"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "0689aec6b08cc26f6b9b0f312c8df0a403a7e915b1a4236e6c0d0425384d475c" "reviewer_session" "01a108cd-e7f4-73f3-b8fc-c82135bc6b7d" "rationale" "For x=2√y−3/√y, dx/dy=y^(-1/2)+(3/2)y^(-3/2). At y=9 this equals 1/3+1/18=7/18, so dy/dx=18/7. The authentic worked solution explicitly reaches 18/7, matching original option b. This is a derived judgment supported by the source, not a successful grade: the saved Incorrect grade concerns submitted 9/5." "bindings" {"problem" "0629593f471942f5e8bc6fcbf2aebae53b5474f094dc5adeb67e44400268fa62" "worked_solution" "4135816d732a6f97952d9bcc312a57bbafb1094a6410a1525909d540c59cf4d9" "original_field" "cafd0fb57299ac28aa459548eb380dc0bb414727671096e639988a4a57f4d7d7" "reviewed_field" "d36a5a8113ffc4540eba9fdf56cfe6cb125c26c3697add691cf973ef219f7f2e" "raw_widget" "37e703d9a78fd4420a34c0176ee6a71c168635ab3f650385e4f59421088d362d"} "evidence_files" [{"path" "q-32595-before.png" "sha256" "485269e6d486579fd32c7867ade9f4e7ecebfe29710d26649f09718a1df4e4cc"} {"path" "history-q-32595.png" "sha256" "6cd29b29e73bedf0c33fcaaa0b620dbef9cab18eb8bb3050dbb7b6a295e7c0c6"} {"path" "history-q-32595.json" "sha256" "77aa35c7f0beb4116e0b553a37a43345695a6485721185d1efc9f9329591c256"}]} {"question" "q-32595" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{18}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{54}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{18}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{5}"]] "category" "reviewed_ma_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977687/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "0689aec6b08cc26f6b9b0f312c8df0a403a7e915b1a4236e6c0d0425384d475c" "rationale" "For x=2√y−3/√y, dx/dy=y^(-1/2)+(3/2)y^(-3/2). At y=9 this equals 1/3+1/18=7/18, so dy/dx=18/7. The authentic worked solution explicitly reaches 18/7, matching original option b. This is a derived judgment supported by the source, not a successful grade: the saved Incorrect grade concerns submitted 9/5."}] "usage" {"e-12468" [] "q-32595" [] "e-12467" [] "q-32705" [] "q-32596" [] "e-12469" []} "basis" 1079 "retractions" [[17592186120133 :question/problem "If $x =-\\frac{2}{y^{2}} + 2y^{2}$, then $\\frac{dy}{dx} =$"] [17592186120126 :question/problem "If $x = 2\\sqrt{y} - \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{y}}$, find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $(5, 9)$."] [17592186120126 :question/answer-fields 17592186117276] [17592186120127 :question/problem "Given a curve $x = \\frac{2}{3}y^{3} - y^{2}$, what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(9, 3)$?"] [17592186119433 :question/problem "If $x=2y^2 + \\dfrac1{y^2}$, then find $\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx}$."] [17592186119433 :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dx}{dy} &= \\frac{d}{dy}(2y^{2} + \\frac{1}{y^{2}}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dy}(2y^{2} + y^{-2}) \\\\\n&= 2\\frac{d}{dy}(y^{2}) + \\frac{d}{dy}(y^{-2}) \\\\\n&= 4y - 2y^{-3} \\\\\n&= 4y - \\frac{2}{y^{3}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{4y^{4} - 2}{y^{3}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx} = \\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy} \\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac{y^3}{4y^4 -2}\n$$"] [17592186119434 :question/problem "If $x = y + 2y\\sqrt y$, find $\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx}$ at the point $\\left(3, 1\\right)$."] [17592186119434 :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dx}{dy} &= \\frac{d}{dy}(y + 2y\\sqrt{y}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dy}(y + 2y^{3/2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dy}(y) + 2\\frac{d}{dy}(y^{3/2}) \\\\\n&= 1 + 2 \\cdot (\\frac{3}{2}y^{1/2}) \\\\\n&= 1 + 3y^{1/2} \\\\\n&= 1 + 3\\sqrt{y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx} = \\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy} \\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac{1}{1 + 3\\sqrt y}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(3,1)$, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(x, y) = (3, 1)} &= \\frac{1}{1 + 3\\sqrt{1}} = \\frac{1}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119435 :question/problem "What is the equation of the tangent to the curve $x = 2y^2 -y + 1$ at the point $(2,1)$?"] [17592186119435 :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dx}{dy} &= \\frac{d}{dy}(2y^{2} - y + 1) \\\\\n&= 2\\frac{d}{dy}(y^{2}) - \\frac{d}{dy}(y) + \\frac{d}{dy}(1) \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot (2y) - 1 + 0 \\\\\n&= 4y - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx} = \\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy} \\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac1{4y - 1}\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(2,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{(x, y) = (2, 1)} \\\\\n&= (1)/(4(1) - 1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - 1 &= \\frac{1}{3}(x - 2) \\\\\ny &= \\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{2}{3} + 1 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{x}{3} + \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186117277 17592186117278 17592186117279 17592186117280 17592186117281 17592186117283 17592186117284 17592186117285 17592186117286 17592186117287 17592186117319 17592186117320 17592186117321 17592186117322 17592186117323] "immutable_fields" [[17592186117276 :answer-field/correct] [17592186117276 :answer-field/id] [17592186117276 :answer-field/key] [17592186117276 :answer-field/type] [17592186117282 :answer-field/correct] [17592186117282 :answer-field/id] [17592186117282 :answer-field/key] [17592186117282 :answer-field/type] [17592186117318 :answer-field/correct] [17592186117318 :answer-field/id] [17592186117318 :answer-field/key] [17592186117318 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
